@prefix cd: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/> .
@prefix ex: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/specifications/level4-applied-moments> {
  ex:l4-applied-mean a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "First moment: the mean locates the data"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Meaning**\n\nThe arithmetic mean is the first raw moment: the balancing point of equally weighted observations. It uses the measurement unit.\n\n**Compare three shapes**\n\n100 synthetic values each: uniform, normal-like and strongly right-skewed. All have mean **50 a.u.**, despite different shapes.\n\nThe next 3×3 panel shows the **same series** as points, a boxplot and a histogram. A cyan line marks the mean in every subplot.\n\n**Limit:** the mean need not be a typical observation and is sensitive to extremes. It does not reveal spread or shape."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-mean-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Population expectation and its empirical counterpart"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}\\mu=\\operatorname{E}[X]\\\\\\bar{x}=\\frac1n\\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_i\\end{gathered}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l4-applied-mean-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l4-source-nist-skew-kurt ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-variance a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Second central moment: variance measures squared spread"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Meaning**\n\nCentre each value on the mean, square the deviation, then average. The result has **squared measurement units** and is unchanged by an additive offset.\n\n**Keep conventions explicit**\n\nDescriptive variance **m₂ uses n**. Sample variance **s² uses n−1**. For our 100-reading series, m₂ = **99 a.u.²** and s² = **100 a.u.²**.\n\nThe next panels shade **mean ± √m₂**, a scale guide in a.u., not variance itself or a fixed-coverage interval.\n\n**Limit:** identical variance can accompany very different shapes; squaring gives extremes substantial influence."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-variance-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Population variance and empirical squared spread"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}\\sigma^2=\\operatorname{E}[(X-\\mu)^2],\\quad\\mu=\\operatorname{E}[X]\\\\m_2=\\frac1n\\sum_i(x_i-\\bar{x})^2=\\frac{n-1}{n}s^2\\end{gathered}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l4-applied-variance-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l4-source-nist-skew-kurt ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-kurtosis a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Kurtosis: weight of extreme standardized deviations"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Meaning**\n\nKurtosis averages fourth powers of deviations after removing location and scale. It is **dimensionless**, not a horizontal coordinate or an interval.\n\n**Compare three shapes**\n\nUniform **K ≈ 1.800**; normal-like **2.834**; right-skewed **6.662**. Excess kurtosis subtracts the normal-population benchmark 3.\n\nIn the next point plots, larger points indicate larger fourth-power contributions. The cyan band is **mean ± two divisor-n SDs**, only a visual scale guide.\n\n**Limit:** kurtosis is not peak height, a mode count or a tail probability. A few extreme values can dominate; m₂ must be positive."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-kurtosis-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Population kurtosis and descriptive sample counterpart"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}\\kappa=\\frac{\\operatorname{E}[(X-\\mu)^4]}{\\sigma^4},\\quad\\sigma>0\\\\K=\\frac{m_4}{m_2^2},\\quad g_2=K-3,\\quad m_2>0\\end{gathered}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l4-applied-kurtosis-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l4-source-nist-skew-kurt ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-skewness a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Skewness: balance of signed cubic deviations"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Meaning**\n\nSkewness standardizes the third central moment. Positive values mean stronger positive cubic contributions; negative values mean stronger negative contributions. It is **dimensionless**.\n\n**Compare three shapes**\n\nUniform and normal-like: g₁ ≈ **0**. Right-skewed: g₁ ≈ **1.759**, with mean 50 above median 46.919 a.u.\n\nThe next panels mark **mean in cyan**, **median in dashed violet**. Point size shows cubic-contribution magnitude; violet/orange distinguishes negative/positive deviations. The coefficient itself is printed, not placed on the measurement axis.\n\n**Limit:** zero skewness does not establish symmetry or a normal distribution."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-skewness-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Population skewness and descriptive sample counterpart"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}\\gamma_1=\\frac{\\operatorname{E}[(X-\\mu)^3]}{\\sigma^3},\\quad\\sigma>0\\\\g_1=\\frac{m_3}{m_2^{3/2}},\\quad m_2>0\\end{gathered}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l4-applied-skewness-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l4-source-nist-skew-kurt ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l4-applied-mean-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l4-am-data, ex:l4-am-mean, ex:l4-am-sum ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-am-data a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "X, xᵢ, i and n"@en ; cd:body "X: random measurement variable; xᵢ: observed value i; i: index 1 to n; n: sample size."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-am-mean a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "μ and x̄"@en ; cd:body "μ: population mean; x̄: mean of this sample. Both use the measurement unit; an observed x̄ need not equal μ."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-am-sum a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "E[ ], Σ and 1/n"@en ; cd:body "E[ ]: probability-weighted population expectation, requiring a finite first absolute moment. Σ adds observations i = 1 to n; 1/n forms their empirical average."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-variance-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l4-av-data, ex:l4-av-m2, ex:l4-av-s2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-av-data a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "X, μ, E[ ] and σ²"@en ; cd:body "X: random measurement; μ: its expectation; E[ ]: population expectation; σ²: population variance. A finite second moment is required."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-av-m2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "m₂ and s²"@en ; cd:body "m₂: empirical variance with divisor n; s²: sample variance with n−1. Their relation requires n > 1. All variances have squared measurement units."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-av-s2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "xᵢ, x̄, n, i and Σ"@en ; cd:body "xᵢ: observed value i; x̄: sample mean; n: sample size; i: index 1 to n; Σ: sum over those observations. The empirical squared deviations concern this sample, not a known population σ²."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-kurtosis-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l4-ak-k, ex:l4-ak-m, ex:l4-ak-g ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ak-k a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "κ, X, μ, σ and E[ ]"@en ; cd:body "κ: population kurtosis; X: random measurement; μ: population mean; σ: population SD; E[ ]: expectation. A finite fourth moment and σ > 0 are required."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ak-m a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "K, m₄ and m₂"@en ; cd:body "K: descriptive sample kurtosis. m₄ and m₂ average fourth and squared deviations from the sample mean, using n. K is dimensionless and requires m₂ > 0."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ak-g a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "g₂ and 3"@en ; cd:body "g₂: sample excess K−3, without bias correction. Population excess: κ−3; 3 is normal-population kurtosis, not every normal sample's value."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-applied-skewness-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l4-as-g, ex:l4-as-m3, ex:l4-as-m2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-as-g a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "γ₁ and g₁"@en ; cd:body "γ₁: population skewness; g₁: descriptive sample counterpart. Both are dimensionless; no small-sample bias adjustment is applied to g₁."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-as-m3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "E[ ], X, μ and σ"@en ; cd:body "E[ ]: population expectation; X: random measurement; μ: population mean; σ: population SD. A finite third absolute moment and σ > 0 are required."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-as-m2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "m₃ and m₂"@en ; cd:body "m₃: average cubed deviation from the sample mean; m₂: average squared deviation, each using n. Dividing by m₂^(3/2) removes the cubed unit. g₁ is undefined if m₂ = 0."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l4-mean-matrix-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Mean: one centre, three distributions and three views"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-variance-matrix-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Variance: identical squared spread does not identify shape"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-kurtosis-matrix-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Kurtosis: follow the extreme-deviation contributions"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-skewness-matrix-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Skewness: distinguish positive and negative contributions"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-mean-matrix a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:ObservationExplorer ; cd:observationView "moments" ; cd:momentMetric "mean" ; skos:prefLabel "Mean in three equivalent views of each series"@en ; cd:body "100 synthetic observations per row; the same observations feed every column. Cyan vertical line: mean. All measurement axes and histogram bins are shared. Point height only separates observations; it is not time or a second measured variable."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Response"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:yAxisLabel "Views"@en ; cd:hasObservationSeries ex:l4-shapes-uniform-series, ex:l4-shapes-normal-series, ex:l4-shapes-skewed-series ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-variance-matrix a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:ObservationExplorer ; cd:observationView "moments" ; cd:momentMetric "variance" ; skos:prefLabel "Descriptive variance across three shapes"@en ; cd:body "100 observations per row. Cyan line: mean; band: mean ± one divisor-n SD (square root of m₂), a scale guide, not a fixed-coverage interval. Printed m₂ has squared units; sample variance s² is 100 a.u.² in each row. Same axes and bins; point height is only separation."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Response"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:yAxisLabel "Views"@en ; cd:hasObservationSeries ex:l4-shapes-uniform-series, ex:l4-shapes-normal-series, ex:l4-shapes-skewed-series ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-kurtosis-matrix a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:ObservationExplorer ; cd:observationView "moments" ; cd:momentMetric "kurtosis" ; skos:prefLabel "Kurtosis and fourth-power contributions"@en ; cd:body "K is a coefficient, not an axis position. Larger points indicate larger fourth-power deviation contributions. Cyan: mean and a ±two divisor-n SD guide; orange points lie outside that guide. It is not a tail-probability interval. Same 100 values, axes and bins per row."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Response"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:yAxisLabel "Views"@en ; cd:hasObservationSeries ex:l4-shapes-uniform-series, ex:l4-shapes-normal-series, ex:l4-shapes-skewed-series ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-skewness-matrix a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:ObservationExplorer ; cd:observationView "moments" ; cd:momentMetric "skewness" ; skos:prefLabel "Skewness and signed cubic contributions"@en ; cd:body "g₁ is printed, not plotted on the measurement axis. Cyan line: mean; dashed violet line: median. Point size indicates cubic-deviation magnitude; violet/orange distinguishes negative/positive deviations. Same 100 values per row, with common measurement axes and histogram bins."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Response"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:yAxisLabel "Views"@en ; cd:hasObservationSeries ex:l4-shapes-uniform-series, ex:l4-shapes-normal-series, ex:l4-shapes-skewed-series ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

